-RIsearch reimplements the RIsearch2 seed-and-extend pipeline.
-Targets are concatenated and indexed in a suffix array, built in linear time by libsais~\citep{libsais}, and each query is scanned against the index for near-complementary seeds, with a configurable number of mismatches and, optionally, G--U wobble pairs (\texttt{-{}-seed-wobble}).
-Seeds are extended in both directions with Gotoh's three-state affine-gap recurrence~\citep{gotoh1982improved}, scoring stacked pairs from a nearest-neighbour dinucleotide model and penalising bulges and internal loops.
-The algorithm and energy model are unchanged, so predicted hybridisation energies match those of RIsearch2.
+RIsearch~(v3) keeps RIsearch2's search algorithm unchanged: targets are concatenated and indexed in a suffix array, then each query is scanned against the index for near-complementary seeds.
+The seeds are then extended in both directions with Gotoh's three-state affine-gap recurrence~\citep{gotoh1982improved}, scoring stacked pairs from a nearest-neighbour dinucleotide model that penalises bulges and internal loops.
+By contrast, the implementation was rewritten from scratch in Rust.
+Most of the code is safe Rust, which guarantees memory safety; unchecked memory access is confined to the performance-critical inner loops of seed search and extension and to the zero-copy loading of the on-disk index.
+The suffix array is now built with libsais~\citep{libsais}, a linear-time construction that can run in parallel across cores, replacing the single-threaded libdivsufsort~\citep{libdivsufsort} used by RIsearch2.
+We regenerated the energy parameter tables from ViennaRNA duplex energies, so the calculated hybridisation energies differ from those of RIsearch2.
 
