+\subsection{Benchmark protocol}\label{sec:benchmark-protocol}
 
 Timing and peak-memory measurements were collected on a server equipped with an AMD EPYC~9554 processor (64 physical cores, 128 threads) and sufficient RAM to keep all input files resident.
 Both pipelines used 32 parallel workers (\texttt{-j~32} for GNU parallel in the legacy case; \texttt{-j~32} process-pool workers for the new pipeline).
 
-For each combination of pipeline version (new / legacy) and batch size (500, 1{,}000, 2{,}000 siRNAs), the following procedure was applied: (i)~one warmup run was executed and discarded to populate OS page-cache entries and JIT any Python bytecode; (ii)~five timed runs were executed, each with a fresh output directory to avoid I/O caching effects.
